  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461600,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this will be callable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462700,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can pass a parameter to this\nand call it like any other function."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466033,
    "dDurationMs": 2567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then I have something like a string,\nwhich of course is not callable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468600,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I run this here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can see we get true for the first four\nand then false for the last one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472933,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next function I have here\nis C or char. Now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475900,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is going to give you the character\nthat's associated with an integer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479333,
    "dDurationMs": 2633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This integer is also referred\nto as the ordinal value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482166,
    "dDurationMs": 4734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this case, 65 represents our capital\nA and 97 represents our lowercase A."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487100,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not necessarily intuitive what number\nrepresents which character continuing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491233,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we print this out, you see that\nwe get a and a because when passed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494466,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "65, it gives us the character\nwhich is capital."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497633,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this is often useful when you want\nto generate a sequence of characters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501333,
    "dDurationMs": 2267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you don't want to say,\nI have to type a bunch of them out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504000,
    "dDurationMs": 2366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I wanted to get\nmaybe the entire alphabet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506500,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or just a bunch of different characters,\nrather than having to type"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509433,
    "dDurationMs": 1833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of them out on my keyboard\nand put them in a list,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511266,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would just increment the ordinal value\nand pass that to my C r function."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515100,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would then give me that character\nand then I could say Auto populate a list"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518166,
    "dDurationMs": 1234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that contains the alphabet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519400,
    "dDurationMs": 2766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next function that I have for\nyou here is class method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522300,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, class method is used as a decorator\non top of a method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525600,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you want to have access to the class,\nnot to the instance itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529333,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whenever you decorate something with that\nclass method by default, be class itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533566,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So actually this class name will be passed\ninside as the class parameter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537700,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You will not have access to the instance,\neven if you call this using an instance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541933,
    "dDurationMs": 1733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can see we have a regular method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543666,
    "dDurationMs": 3934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This regular method just prints itself,\nwhich is going to go to this string method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547600,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right here that I implemented."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548900,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can see when I say T equals\ntest class and then t dot regular method"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552600,
    "dDurationMs": 1966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it prints out my test instance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554566,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas when I call the class method,\neither on my instance or on the class"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558100,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "itself, both are valid\nand do the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560333,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I actually get the class\nwhen I print it out because it's not using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563900,
    "dDurationMs": 3066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the representation of the object\nor of the instance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567500,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, we have a complex."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568833,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, I don't really know\nmuch about complex numbers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570833,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this is how you can generate\ncomplex numbers."
