  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094333,
    "dDurationMs": 767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I look here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095100,
    "dDurationMs": 3666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the help on the INT class,\nthen you can see I get all of this data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099033,
    "dDurationMs": 2067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next function that I have here\nis known as Hex."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101100,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, this stands for hexadecimal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102633,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's going to give you the hexadecimal\nrepresentation of an integer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this only works on a class\nthat implements the underscore underscore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109200,
    "dDurationMs": 1166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "index method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110366,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if we create a custom class\nthat implements index, this will work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113700,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just going to return the hex value of\nwhatever is returned by index."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118100,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this case, when I run this,\nI get 0f0x1 in 0xa,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122366,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the correct hexadecimal codes\nfor 255 one and then 410,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1127300,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is returned when I call this on C\nbecause it calls the index method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131400,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The next function I have is known as ID."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133400,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now this is going to give me the\nidentifier for a specific python object."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136833,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is very useful if you want to check\nif two objects are the same or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140366,
    "dDurationMs": 2567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this case I have my mutable list."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142933,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I then assign y equals to x."
